-- title:
--   Deligne's ordinary eigenline at p in weight two
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, let $N\ge 1$ satisfy $p\nmid N$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\notin S$, let $k=2$ as an integer and $kn$ a natural number with $(kn:\mathbb Z)=k$ (so $kn-1=1$). Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\theta$ a ring homomorphism from `heckeAlgebra N k S`, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_k(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$, to $F$, with $\theta(T_p)\neq 0$. Let $\rho:\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be a monoid homomorphism that is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension $L/\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ pointwise, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma)=\theta(T_\ell)$ and $\det\rho(\sigma)=\ell^{kn-1}$; assume further that $\rho$ is absolutely irreducible in the sense that for every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $e:F\to F'$ and every nonzero $u\in F'^2$ there is a $\sigma$ with $(e\rho(\sigma))u\notin F'u$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a nonunit. Then there are a field $F'$, a ring homomorphism $e:F\to F'$, a homomorphism $\rho':\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(F')$ and $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(F')$ with $\rho'(\sigma)=g\,(e\rho(\sigma))\,g^{-1}$ for all $\sigma$, and a nonzero $v'\in F'^2$ such that: $F'v'$ is stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$; for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ (the image of the inertia subgroup in the decomposition subgroup) and all $w$, $\rho'(\sigma)w-w\in F'v'$; for every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group acting as $x\mapsto x^p$ on the residue field of $P$ and all $w$, $\rho'(\sigma)w-e(\theta(T_p))w\in F'v'$; and for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup and $a\in\mathbb N$ with $\sigma\mu=\mu^a$ for all $p$-th roots of unity $\mu$, $\rho'(\sigma)v'=a^{kn-1}v'$.
--
--   This is Deligne's description, in weight two and for a non-zero $T_p$-eigenvalue, of the restriction to a decomposition group at $p$ of the mod $p$ representation attached to a Hecke eigensystem: after a conjugation over an extension of scalars the representation is reducible on the decomposition group at $p$, with unramified quotient on which Frobenius acts by $\theta(T_p)$ and with inertia acting on the stable line through the mod $p$ cyclotomic character to the power $k-1$. It feeds the ordinariness statement [`GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_two`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_two), which is the form of the $p$-adic local condition used in the modularity-lifting argument.
